  "title": "Discovery Engine: Notebook Scoping, Field Matching, & Feedback Enhancements",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine gains new capabilities for federated search data stores, allowing restriction to specific notebooks. Developers can now configure partial and prefix matching for fields, and feedback tracking gets more granular with new conversation info.",
  "details": "Developers using Discovery Engine's federated search can now precisely control data store scope. The `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreFederatedSearchConfigNotebooklmConfig` (and its alpha/beta counterparts) introduces a new `notebooks` array property. This allows you to restrict a data store to specific notebook resources, ensuring search results are confined to relevant content.\n\nFor fine-tuning search relevance, the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfig` schema now includes `partialMatchableOption` and `prefixMatchableOption`. These new enum fields provide granular control over how field values are matched during searches, enabling more precise indexing and query behavior.\n\nFeedback mechanisms have also been enhanced. The `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackConversationInfo` schema gains `stepSeqNum` and `trajectoryId` properties, offering more detailed context for agent task turns. Additionally, `GOOGLE_AGENTSPACE_DESKTOP` is now a recognized `feedbackSource` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Feedback`.",
